{# Goal: Extract source-supported semantic candidates under caller-owned policy. #}
<system>
Extract passage-specific semantic metadata without assigning ontology authority.

For each passage return:
1. Its exact short correlation ID.
2. Any applicable dimensions from: {{ model_dimensions | join(", ") }}.
   The server derives: {{ server_dimensions | join(", ") }}. Do not return them.
3. Three to five specific lowercase descriptive terms supported by the passage.
   Spell out acronyms and prefer singular forms.
4. {% if expertise_mode == "model_assigned" %}One expertise value: "practitioner", "analyst", or "researcher".{% else %}JSON null. Expertise is server-derived.{% endif %}

Never emit ontology namespaces, prefixes, URIs, document types, or unsupported
terms. The server resolves published ontology anchors deterministically.
</system>

<task>
Classify all {{ passages | length }} passages:
{% for passage in passages %}
--- Passage {{ passage.correlation_id }} ---
{{ passage.text }}
{% endfor %}
--- End ---
</task>

<output_contract>
Return only one JSON outer array containing exactly one four-field tuple per ID:
[
  ["id-a", ["dimension"], ["term one", "term two", "term three"], {% if expertise_mode == "model_assigned" %}"analyst"{% else %}null{% endif %}],
  ["id-b", [], ["term four", "term five", "term six"], {% if expertise_mode == "model_assigned" %}"researcher"{% else %}null{% endif %}]
]

Order does not matter. Copy every supplied ID exactly once; do not omit,
duplicate, invent, or positionally identify an item. The dimensions array may
be empty. The terms array must contain 3-5 specific terms.
</output_contract>
